{
  "analysis": "Read-only comparison of the prior profitable recurrent stage2 case and newly measured pipeline slowdowns",
  "native_library_sha256": "e7e15b9337405e632e887ceae9c96d9ea85e38aa1e9c35dec937d7b148d06178",
  "gpu_runs_performed_for_this_analysis": false,
  "native_changes": false,
  "conclusions": [
    "Two stages do not imply useful compute/read-ahead overlap. The profitable T63 and T500 recurrent loops also have one-slot shared allocations and wait0/local-load/compute/store/next-copy TTGIR ordering. Their PTX issues next-iteration copies after the output store.",
    "Stage2 changes layout transport as well as timing. Recurrent q and k each feed two register layouts. Baseline uses convert_layout for each after normalization; the transformed code loads each shared tensor directly into both layouts, eliminating those two explicit conversions.",
    "At the same BV8/one-warp/launch-stages3 configuration, T63 improves 1.207-1.210x over three fresh confirmations. Registers change only 64 to 63, shared bytes increase 256 to 724, and neither variant spills. This rules out changed launch selection as the sole source of that gain.",
    "On the audited T63 PTX loop path, baseline executes three CTA barrier sites and three warp barrier sites per iteration. Pipeline executes two CTA sites and one warp site per iteration, plus async wait/commit work. Its two remaining CTA barriers are outside the recurrent loop. Four explicit scalar shared-store sites for q/k layout conversion disappear; the output-conversion shared store remains.",
    "The new log-softmax and rotary cases have zero explicit convert_layout operations before and after staging, so this specific offsetting benefit is absent. Upsample retains all eight explicit conversions, which already lower without shared stores or barriers at this launch.",
    "The layout/synchronization changes are a code-based explanation, not a causally isolated attribution. Grouping scalar loads into async copies, L1 cache behavior, instruction scheduling, and data layout can also contribute. No recurrent counter profile or direct layout-only ablation was performed here."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "The PTX counts are source instruction sites, not measured dynamic hardware counters. Per-iteration counts follow the inspected recurrent loop control flow; whole-file totals include epilogues.",
    "Retained PTX and TTGIR do not establish the final SASS scheduling or latency overlap by themselves.",
    "T500 fresh confirmations compare independently selected BV32/w2 baseline with BV8/w1 pipeline; only its earlier screening measurements compare BV8/w1 directly. T63 confirms identical baseline and pipeline launch configurations.",
    "The profitable stage2 examples prevent a universal claim that one-slot stage2 is useless. Profitability depends on the other transformations induced by staging and on workload/launch geometry."
  ],
